Description: fall back to the recorded upstream commit when git is unavailable
 In the pxvirt Docker build the ceph packaging repo is a git submodule whose
 .git is a gitfile pointing into the parent repository, which is not part of
 the build context. `git rev-parse HEAD` therefore prints nothing, the
 Makefile writes an empty first line into src/.git_version and every binary
 reports "ceph version 20.2.1 () tentacle". Proxmox VE's parser
 (PVE::Ceph::Tools::parse_ceph_version) requires a commit hash inside the
 parentheses; with the empty one, get_local_version() returns undef and the
 GUI/API refuse to set up Ceph with "Ceph Nautilus required - please run
 'pveceph install'". Use the commit recorded in ceph/src/.git_version instead.
Author: pxvirt
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ SRCDIR=ceph
 BUILDSRC=${SRCDIR}-${VER}
 
 ARCH:=$(shell dpkg-architecture -qDEB_BUILD_ARCH)
-GITVERSION:=$(shell git rev-parse HEAD)
+GITVERSION:=$(shell git rev-parse HEAD 2>/dev/null || head -n1 ${SRCDIR}/src/.git_version)
 
 DBG_DEBS=ceph-common-dbg_${PKGVER}_${ARCH}.deb \
 ceph-fuse-dbg_${PKGVER}_${ARCH}.deb \
